---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="About - Tushar Roy">
    <main class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pt-32 pb-16">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center mb-32">
            <h2 class="heading-medium mb-8 leading-tight">
                Engineer at heart,<br /> Product Designer by calling.
            </h2>
            <p
                class="text-[var(--color-text-primary)] text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed mb-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto"
            >
                I design enterprise platforms by <em class="font-sans"
                    >making complexity understandable</em
                >, both for users <u
                    class="decoration-[var(--color-accent)] decoration-2 underline-offset-4"
                    >and for teams building them</u
                >. Here's how..
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Philosophy Blocks -->
        <section class="mb-32">
            <div class="space-y-32">
                <!-- Block 1: Strategy -->
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-24 items-center">
                    <div class="order-2 md:order-1">
                        <div class="eyebrow-sm mb-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]">
                            The Strategy
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium mb-6">
                            Context is Everything
                        </h3>
                        <p
                            class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] text-lg leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            I approach design challenges as a puzzle, where the
                            winning strategy comes from connecting the dots
                            between users, business, and systems. When those
                            align, everyone wins.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="order-1 md:order-2">
                        <img
                            src="/images/about-tr-design.png"
                            alt="Design Strategy"
                            class="block mx-auto"
                        />
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Block 2: Process -->
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-24 items-center">
                    <div class="order-1">
                        <img
                            src="/images/about-tr-outreach.png"
                            alt="Playful Process"
                            class="block mx-auto"
                        />
                    </div>
                    <div class="order-2">
                        <div class="eyebrow-sm mb-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]">
                            The Process
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium mb-6">Play as Purpose</h3>
                        <p
                            class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] text-lg leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            The path forward is not always obvious. I use a
                            mindset of curiosity and play to guide teams from
                            "unknown to clarity," uncovering unexpected
                            opportunities along the way.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Block 3: Leadership -->
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-24 items-center">
                    <div class="order-2 md:order-1">
                        <div class="eyebrow-sm mb-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]">
                            Leadership
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium mb-6">
                            The Team Sport Called Design
                        </h3>
                        <p
                            class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] text-lg leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            With only 8 designers in a 2,000+ person
                            organization at VMware, I learned that the best
                            outcomes happen when design is a collaborative
                            effort. I built maturity programs that scaled impact
                            beyond the design team - reinforcing my belief that
                            design is a shared responsibility where everyone
                            plays, solves, and grows together.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="order-1 md:order-2">
                        <img
                            src="/images/about-tr-team.png"
                            alt="Team Collaboration"
                            class="block mx-auto"
                        />
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Block 4: Perspective -->
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-24 items-center">
                    <div class="order-1">
                        <img
                            src="/images/about-tr-vmops.png"
                            alt="Accessible Design"
                            class="block mx-auto"
                        />
                    </div>
                    <div class="order-2">
                        <div class="eyebrow-sm mb-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]">
                            An Unique Perspective
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium mb-6">
                            The Accessible Advantage
                        </h3>
                        <p
                            class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] text-lg leading-relaxed"
                        >
                            I came to design not for how it looks, but for how
                            well it works. As a colorblind designer (and
                            developer), accessibility isn't just a checklist -
                            it’s a lived constraint. This perspective drives me
                            to build experiences that are usable, resilient, and
                            inclusive by default.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
</Layout>
